# Copy to `.env` and fill in values.

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Dashboard login (optional)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# HOW YOU CREATE THE LOGIN (as the host / operator)
# -----------------------------------------------
# 1. Pick any Login ID you want (e.g. acme_fund or jane.doe).
# 2. Pick a strong password (long random string or passphrase).
# 3. Put them here:
#      DASHBOARD_CLIENT_ID=<your Login ID>
#      DASHBOARD_CLIENT_SECRET=<your password>
# 4. Deploy / restart the API so it loads the new .env.
# 5. Share with the person who should access the dashboard:
#      - URL: your frontend (e.g. https://your-app.com/login)
#      - Login ID: same as DASHBOARD_CLIENT_ID
#      - Password: same as DASHBOARD_CLIENT_SECRET
#
# They open /login, enter those two values, then use /dashboard and "Run analysis".
#
# NOTE: The API still expects JSON field names `client_id` and `client_secret`;
# the UI labels them "Login ID" and "Password". Same values.
#
# Leave EITHER variable empty to turn login OFF (typical local dev — no password).
#
DASHBOARD_CLIENT_ID=
DASHBOARD_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Sign session tokens (use a long random string in production).
# If unset, a key is derived from DASHBOARD_CLIENT_SECRET.
# API_AUTH_SIGNING_SECRET=

# Session length in seconds (default 7 days).
# DASHBOARD_TOKEN_TTL_SECONDS=604800

# Persistent monthly metric cache (used when timeframe=month)
# Enable to avoid re-fetching low-frequency macro series every run.
# ENABLE_MONTHLY_METRIC_CACHE=1
# MONTHLY_SLOW_METRIC_CACHE_TTL_SECONDS=43200
